{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://firecraw.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Firecrawl MCP","item":"https://firecraw.com/firecrawl-mcp"}]}{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"Firecrawl MCP for AI agents","description":"Firecrawl MCP gives a compatible AI client a tool-shaped way to request web content. The useful question is which agent needs which web operation, and how you will control the key.","url":"https://firecraw.com/firecrawl-mcp","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Firecraw Tools"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Firecraw Tools"},"dateModified":"2026-09-20"}Agent integrationFirecrawl MCP for AI agents
Firecrawl MCP gives a compatible AI client a tool-shaped way to request web content. The useful question is which agent needs which web operation, and how you will control the key.
What Firecrawl MCP adds
Model Context Protocol lets an AI client discover callable tools. A Firecrawl MCP server can expose web actions such as search, scrape, crawl, and extraction so the agent can ask for current context during a task.
Configuration pattern
MCP client configuration{
  class="tok-string">"mcpServers": {
    class="tok-string">"firecrawl": {
      class="tok-string">"command": class="tok-string">"npx",
      class="tok-string">"args": [class="tok-string">"-y", class="tok-string">"firecrawl-mcp"],
      class="tok-string">"env": {
        class="tok-string">"FIRECRAWL_API_KEY": class="tok-string">"your_key_here"
      }
    }
  }
}Package names, transport options, and client configuration can change. Use the current provider instructions alongside this pattern and never commit a real key.
Good first workflows

- Ask an agent to research a known set of documentation pages.
- Let a coding agent inspect current API references before suggesting code.
- Extract a small set of fields from a public page with a reviewed schema.Firecrawl MCP guardrails
Limit allowed domains where possible, ask for confirmation before expensive crawls, and treat retrieved text as untrusted input. MCP expands access; it does not make web content authoritative.
 Frequently asked questions
What is Firecrawl MCP?It is an MCP server pattern that lets compatible AI clients call web retrieval tools through a tool interface.
How does Firecrawl MCP handle web content?Firecrawl MCP exposes retrieval tools, but retrieved content remains untrusted input and should be validated before an agent acts on it.
